{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "2b3c4d5e-6f7a-4b8c-9d0e-1f2a3b4c5d6e",
    "name": "LedgerOne - Inventory (Unit)",
    "description": "Inventory module (Unit of Measure) API collection (Create, Get, Update, List by Company, List Base Units). Reflects the implementation exactly as shipped in apps/api/src/shared/inventory.\n\nDesign note (tenant-owned, X-Tenant-Id always required; header rewrite): identical posture to ProductCategory.postman_collection.json — every /api/v1/inventory/* route sits behind jwt-auth.middleware.ts AND current-tenant.middleware.ts mounted with `{ rewriteHeaderAs: \"decimal\" }` (module-registry.ts), which overwrites `x-tenant-id` in place with the verified JWT claim before this module's own tenantIdHeaderSchema ever inspects it — so a missing/malformed X-Tenant-Id does not itself fail validation here either (mirrors Exchange Rate's documented behavior). No dedicated 'missing/malformed X-Tenant-Id' failure case is included for the same reason.\n\nDesign note (response omits baseUnitUuid, a documented Handbook Deviation, not a bug): unit.response.dto.ts deliberately omits `baseUnitUuid` from the response entirely (an extra Repository lookup per row, mirroring Product Category's own `parentProductCategoryUuid` omission) — not tested for presence or absence beyond the PK-003 internal-field checks.\n\nDesign note (route ordering, documentation only): apps/api/src/shared/inventory/index.ts registers `GET /units/base-units` (a static path) BEFORE `GET /units/:unitUuid` (a param route) deliberately — Express matches routes in registration order, so the literal segment must come first or every request for it would instead match `:unitUuid=\"base-units\"`. This collection's own folder mirrors that same order (List Base Units request appears before the Get-by-uuid requests) purely as documentation; Postman itself has no route-registration-order concept, this is not load-bearing for the collection to function.\n\nDesign note (no name/symbol uniqueness rule): unlike Product Category's Ch.35.8, the handbook defines no Unit name/symbol uniqueness rule (create-unit.service.ts's own header comment) — this collection therefore includes no 'Duplicate Name' test for Unit, a deliberate omission mirroring the source's own documented gap, not an oversight.\n\nDesign note (conversionFactor validation, Ch.36.8): 'Conversion factor must be a positive number' — enforced once by the Business layer (isPositiveDecimalString), not duplicated as a Zod regex. This collection tests all three non-positive/malformed shapes (\"0\", \"-5\", \"not-a-number\") against the same INV_INVALID_UNIT_CONVERSION_FACTOR_VALUE code.\n\nThere is no delete endpoint for Unit, so a collection-level pre-request script derives a `{{unitSuffix}}` from the current timestamp (once per Newman invocation) appended to every created name, avoiding cross-run collisions on the `uq_units_tenant_company_name_deleted_at` composite the Database milestone added (flagged in create-unit.service.ts as a raw, untyped Prisma unique-constraint violation if triggered through this service — this collection's own generated names avoid ever exercising that gap).\n\nRun order for a full pass, top to bottom: {{baseUnitUuid}} must be set (by 'Create Base Unit - Success') before 'Create Alternate Unit - Success' (which references it), and both before the Get/Update/List requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
